{
  "calendar": "KR",
  "about": "Korean won (KRW) settlement calendar: weekdays when Seoul banks are closed and BOK-Wire+ does not settle, taken as the public holidays of the Regulation on Holidays of Government Offices (관공서의 공휴일에 관한 규정) / Public Holidays Act plus Workers' Day. Rules: Jan 1; Seollal and Chuseok (eve, day, day after, by the Korean lunar calendar); Mar 1; May 1 (Workers' Day 2010-2025, a bank holiday on which banks, KRX and the Seoul FX market close though it was not a public holiday; Labour Day, a public holiday by the 2026 amendment approved by the Cabinet on 28 Apr 2026); May 5; Buddha's Birthday; Jun 6; Jul 17 (Constitution Day, restored as a public holiday from 2026, not one 2010-2025); Aug 15; Oct 3; Oct 9 (Hangul Day, from 2013); Dec 25. Substitute holidays are not a simple weekend rule (Seollal/Chuseok only when they overlap a Sunday or another holiday, since 2014; Children's Day on a weekend from 2014; Mar 1, Aug 15, Oct 3, Oct 9 from 2021; Buddha's Birthday and Christmas from May 2023; Labour Day and Constitution Day from 2026; never Jan 1 or Memorial Day), so they are dated tables. Election days (statutory holidays) and cabinet-designated temporary holidays are cited exceptions. Dec 31 is NOT a closure: KRX and the Seoul interbank FX market (서울외환시장운영협의회) close for year-end, but banks keep normal hours and customer FX continues, so BOK-Wire+/bank settlement is open. Checked against: KASI/우주항공청 2027 월력요항 data (exact match, published 29 Jun 2026); KASI 2023 Korean Astronomical Almanac (matches, plus 2023-05-29 and 2023-10-02 added after it went to print); kholidayz.com's 2026 list (exact match; an aggregator, with the Labour Day and Constitution Day change confirmed by Newsis and Money Today reports of the 28 Apr 2026 Cabinet decision). The lunar dates for 2010-2026 and the substitute dates for 2017-2025 come from the vacanza/holidays dataset (rule-derived), cross-checked against an independent KASI-standard lunar conversion table (usingsky/korean_lunar_calendar_py) and spot-checked against press reports (2014-09-10, 2015-09-29, 2016-02-10, 2023-05-29); they were not each read from a KASI page here. Covers 2010-2027. 2027's temporary holidays aren't known yet (none designated as of Oct 2026); 2026 is complete as of Oct 2026 (2026-09-28 was proposed but not designated). KASI has posted unofficial 2028 data; 2028 is not covered until the official 월력요항 is out.",
